All of my comments apply to version 3.1.1 as I haven't yet acquired
3.1.3.  I don't have any reason to believe that things are any different
in the latter version, however.

Anyway, weapons can be safely enchanted up to +5.  In addition, one
enchantment that takes the weapon past +5 can be safely performed. 
Thus, the way to ensure a maximum enchantment is to get your weapon to
+5 and then read a blessed scroll of enchant weapon.

>>Also my gauntlets of dexterity vibrated violently at +4. ????
> 
>It means it's gonna blow next time.

Yup.  As of 3.1, stuff gets one chance to fail an enchantment.  This is
the "vibrate violently" message.  Don't push your luck at that point.

Also, while I'm thinking about it, unless things have changed (I haven't
looked at the source for 3.1.x) the chance to enchant weapons is a flat
1/3 past +5, while the chance to successfully enchant armor goes down
continually.  Thus, you're far more likely to get a +10 weapon than a
+10 piece of armor.  I have actually had +10 weapons before (usually by
accident), so I know it can be done, while I've never seen better than
+5 armor.

